    {
      "id": "b451187784e9507e85a32260",
      "title": "‘I grew my hair and dropped out of society after hearing Black Sabbath’: J Mascis’s honest playlist",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2026/sep/13/honest-playlist-j-mascis-dinosaur-jr-black-sabbath-nwa-tom-petty",
      "summary": "The Dinosaur Jr axe man stole from his mum to buy a Beach Boys record and squeaks to Tom Petty – but which punk banger made him cry? What’s the first song you fell in love with? Monster Mash by Bobby “Boris” Pickett. Monsters appealed to me as a kid. I found it funny, not spooky. Since I had a kid, Halloween has become the biggest holiday of the year. What was the first single you bought? I bought Darlin’ by the Beach Boys with the money I would steal from my mom. I always liked the Beach Boys. I remember they were quite unhip for a while: I played them at a gig around 1989 before we came on a",
